.\"##
.\"
.\" Manual page of "mcp-python-compose" - the launcher of the MCP server
.\" "mcp-python" by Docker Compose, for the current user. The secrets, the
.\" environment and the security - in "mcp-python-container.1", the same
.\" for both launchers.
.\"
.\" View the source: man ./container/mcp-python-compose.1
.TH MCP-PYTHON-COMPOSE 1 2026-11-15 "mcp-python-container" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mcp-python-compose \- the MCP server mcp-python of the current user, by Docker Compose
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcp-python-compose up
.RI [ "docker compose up options" ]
.br
.B mcp-python-compose
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.br
.B mcp-python-compose
.RB { \-h | \-\-help }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mcp-python-compose
starts the
.BR mcp-python (8)
server - an MCP server, which runs a Python 3 code for its clients - in a
container of the local Docker, as a service of the user who runs it, with
Docker Compose: in the background, back after a restart of Docker or of
the host. A Compose project per user. The same server in the foreground -
.BR mcp-python-container (1).
.PP
HTTPS at port
.BR 8766 ,
published at
.B 127.0.0.1
of the host
.RB ( MCP_PUBLISH_HOST ).
.PP
The arguments are a command of
.B docker compose
for the project of the user, with its arguments. Nothing is started
without a command.
.TP
.B up
Starts the server, in the background -
.BR "docker compose up \-\-detach" .
Before it - the secrets and the image, as
.BR mcp-python-container (1)
describes.
.TP
.BR start ", " restart ", " create ", " run
As
.BR "docker compose" ,
the secrets and the image first too.
.TP
.BR down ", " stop ", " logs ", " ps ", ..."
As
.BR "docker compose" .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/mcp-python-container/docker-compose.yml
The container - the image, the listener, the mounts of the secrets, the
limits.
.PP
The secrets of the user - see
.BR mcp-python-container (1),
FILES.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The same as of
.BR mcp-python-container (1),
besides
.BR "docker compose" 's own.
.SH SECURITY
The same as of
.BR mcp-python-container (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
The server, in the background, and its log:
.PP
.RS
.EX
mcp-python-compose up
mcp-python-compose logs \-\-follow
.EE
.RE
.PP
One more client - its token in
.IR ~/.local/share/mcp-python/clients/laptop.token :
.PP
.RS
.EX
MCP_CLIENT=laptop mcp-python-compose restart
.EE
.RE
.PP
A client removed:
.PP
.RS
.EX
rm ~/.local/share/mcp-python/tokens/laptop \e
   ~/.local/share/mcp-python/clients/laptop.token
mcp-python-compose restart
.EE
.RE
.PP
Stop and remove:
.PP
.RS
.EX
mcp-python-compose down
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mcp-python-container (1),
.BR mcp-python (8),
.BR docker-compose (1),
.BR curl (1)
